<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">WQS26: Workshop on Quantum Software 2026</div><div id="cfpvenue">QTML 2026</div><div id="cfpdateplace">Stellenbosh, South Africa, December 12, 2026</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://data-cybernetics.com/en/wqs-2026" target="_blank">https://data-cybernetics.com/en/wqs-2026</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=wqs26" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=wqs26</a></td></tr><tr><td>Abstract registration deadline</td><td>September 1, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>September 8, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Submission Format</td><td>Maximum of 5-page (excluded references) extended abstract.</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=18135" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_blue bg_gray1">programming language design</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=11298" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_bluelight bg_yellow">compilers</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=838" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_bluelight bg_darkyellow">formal methods</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=98094" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_blue bg_aqua">program analysis and verification</span></a></div><h2>Description</h2>

<p>Quantum software development is becoming a critical skill as quantum computing matures from theory to practice. The Workshop on Quantum Software (WQS) addresses all the intermediate layers of the quantum computing stack, from high-level algorithms down to hardware implementation.</p>

<p>WQS addresses four pillars of quantum software, namely:</p>

<p>- <span style="color:#d35400"><em>Language Design</em></span>: High-level programming language definition through machine-independent syntax and semantics specifications for quantum computation.</p>

<p>- <span style="color:#d35400"><em>Compilation</em></span>: Structured methodologies for translating high-level quantum programs into executable form, bridging the gap between abstraction and hardware.</p>

<p>- <span style="color:#d35400"><em>Formal Methods</em></span>: Analysis of program properties, verification techniques, and compiler optimization, ensuring correctness in quantum software.</p>

<p>- <span style="color:#d35400"><em>Support Software for Quantum Computers</em></span>:&nbsp;Bridging compiled quantum programs and physical execution, translating abstract operations into hardware, managing the precise orchestration required for reliable operation.</p>

<h2>Submission</h2>

<p>We solicit submissions in the form of a maximum of 5-page (excluded references) extended abstracts describing original results in the form of ongoing works potentially able to foster interesting and constructive discussions. Work already published will also be considered for discussion. In this case, we invite the authors to clearly state this in their submission by indicating the reference to the journal/conference where it was published and the link to the full paper, wherever possible.</p>

<p>There is no fixed format to prepare your submission, but we recommend the use of a single-column layout with a no less than 10pt size.</p>

<h2>Contact</h2>

<p><a href="mailto:alessandra.dipierro@univr.it">Alessandra Di Pierro</a>&nbsp;and <a href="mailto:blank@data-cybernetics.com">Carsten Blank</a></p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
